The source checkout contains runtime source metadata but not the third-party
runtime archive. A provider release includes the adjacent archive named by
runtime/release.json. runtime/sources.json records the precise versions, source
locations and hashes for its pinned inputs:

- wechat-local-agent-mcp, maintained by hetiankong
- wechat-cli and wxkey, maintained by R266 Tech
- Tencent's SQLCipher fork
- CPython via Astral's python-build-standalone distribution

The runtime artifact has its own third-party licenses and file receipt. Preserve
those notices when distributing that artifact; this notice does not replace
upstream license texts. The runtime build also includes its Go runtime and Python
dependencies, whose notices belong with that artifact. The release build checks
the archive's pinned SHA-256; installation independently checks the archive and
its file receipt.

An official public release URL is recorded in runtime/release.json only when an
asset has been published. Provider and Worka release builds verify a local
runtime cache before fetching a published, exact pinned URL, then copy the
archive beside the provider. A local build uses runtime/build.mjs and the
hash-pinned inputs, patches and toolchains documented with the receipt; it does
not invent a download URL. Explicit deployment overrides remain available.
Recording wxkey as runtime provenance does not invoke key extraction.
